1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,307
In 1971, two dozen

2
00:00:01,307 --> 00:00:02,832
students were locked in

3
00:00:02,832 --> 00:00:04,401
a basement at Stanford.

4
00:00:04,401 --> 00:00:05,745
It became the most

5
00:00:05,745 --> 00:00:08,040
famous experiment in psychology.

6
00:00:08,490 --> 00:00:09,819
You know the ending.

7
00:00:09,819 --> 00:00:11,948
Within days, ordinary students

8
00:00:11,948 --> 00:00:13,277
playing guards turned cruel.

9
00:00:13,277 --> 00:00:14,556
The study was shut

10
00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:15,885
down after six days.

11
00:00:16,235 --> 00:00:17,704
The lesson seemed obvious.

12
00:00:17,704 --> 00:00:18,792
Put good people in

13
00:00:18,792 --> 00:00:19,922
a bad system, and

14
00:00:19,922 --> 00:00:21,162
they become monsters.

15
00:00:21,562 --> 00:00:22,925
For almost fifty years,

16
00:00:22,925 --> 00:00:24,467
textbooks taught exactly that.

17
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:26,117
But in 2018, a

18
00:00:26,117 --> 00:00:27,494
French researcher went back

19
00:00:27,494 --> 00:00:29,103
into the archives. The

20
00:00:29,103 --> 00:00:30,572
tapes. The notes. The

21
00:00:30,572 --> 00:00:31,242
interviews.

22
00:00:31,591 --> 00:00:32,506
And the story started

23
00:00:32,506 --> 00:00:32,871
to crack.

24
00:00:33,571 --> 00:00:34,894
On one recording, a

25
00:00:34,894 --> 00:00:36,026
staff member pushes a

26
00:00:36,026 --> 00:00:37,043
guard to be tougher.

27
00:00:37,043 --> 00:00:38,022
The guards weren't left

28
00:00:38,022 --> 00:00:39,537
alone. They were coached.

29
00:00:39,987 --> 00:00:41,246
Then the prisoner whose

30
00:00:41,246 --> 00:00:42,505
breakdown made the study

31
00:00:42,505 --> 00:00:44,064
famous said something nobody

32
00:00:44,064 --> 00:00:44,603
expected.

33
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:45,848
He said he was

34
00:00:45,848 --> 00:00:47,085
faking. He wanted out,

35
00:00:47,085 --> 00:00:48,086
so he could study

36
00:00:48,086 --> 00:00:48,916
for his exams.

37
00:00:49,616 --> 00:00:50,524
So was it all

38
00:00:50,524 --> 00:00:52,020
fake? Not quite. Some

39
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:53,096
guards really did turn

40
00:00:53,096 --> 00:00:54,046
harsh. And the man

41
00:00:54,046 --> 00:00:55,290
who ran it defended

42
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:56,409
it until he died.

43
00:00:56,809 --> 00:00:57,864
The real lesson might

44
00:00:57,864 --> 00:00:59,125
be darker. People don't

45
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:00,345
just become cruel on

46
00:01:00,345 --> 00:01:01,277
their own. They do

47
00:01:01,277 --> 00:01:02,497
it when someone in

48
00:01:02,497 --> 00:01:03,717
charge makes it clear

49
00:01:03,717 --> 00:01:04,978
that's what is expected.

50
00:01:05,428 --> 00:01:06,531
Which raises a question

51
00:01:06,531 --> 00:01:08,380
about every famous experiment

52
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:09,521
you were ever taught.

53
00:01:09,921 --> 00:01:11,528
Next file: thirty-eight witnesses

54
00:01:11,528 --> 00:01:12,792
watched a crime and

55
00:01:12,792 --> 00:01:14,100
did nothing. That story

56
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:15,005
isn't true either.
